host Ubuntu 26.04 LTS GNOME Wayland (Framework 16 AMD) — Eastern (EDT) time convention
title Mycelium Knot r1 — a bounded Cord ties off its committed past; checkpoint folds identical to the whole history
prompt Take the next agent-doable lap Lindy-first crux-first; approve own design rounds and make progress before checking in; double-seat visions; send each increment as its own signed round; stop only at custody gates
think Read REMEMBER + the 1024-round itinerary + the six-season double-seat. The Mycelium consensus arc (Season D) had closed three 4-round arcs: the Cord (deterministic leaderless commit), gossip convergence (partition heal), and fact batching (throughput). The batching arc's own tail named the next crux as a fresh Season D journey.
think The highest-Lindy crux left on the Mycelium road: the Cord's Dag is statically allocated (cord_max_blocks 256) — a TigerBeetle feature, yet a bound reached is a mesh that stops. Every long-lived deterministic state machine checkpoints: fold the committed past into a summary, prune it, continue from the summary. Without it the bounded Dag is a demo; with it, the same bounded Dag runs forever. That is the durable, still-tractable, agent-doable next crux.
think Named it the Knot (comlink-tendency: clear·fun·safe) — a knot ties off a length of cord and begins the next; grepped zero collisions in mycelium/ mantra/ pond/ tally/ comlink/ and the Lexicon. Fits the Cord family exactly.
think The property that makes it safe, found by reading fold.fold_fact: the whole supply law lives in the FoldState it mutates (non-negative supply refuses Overdraw against state.supply(); star-uniqueness refuses StarTaken against the state's stars; each fact re-verifies its own signer). So seeding the fold from a sealed checkpoint carries all three invariants across the cut — the Knot is not a shortcut around the law but the law's own state, sealed.
think Grew mycelium/cord_knot.rye BESIDE the elder (cord.rye and fold.rye stay green binaries; composes their public API only). A Knot = the folded FoldState at a committed cut under a streaming SHA-256 digest (no signature — a Knot is a deterministic function of the committed Dag; the digest is integrity-in-travel, never authority). seal_dag commits + flattens + folds + seals; continue_verified folds a next-epoch log onto a verified Knot.
think The crux on metal: a prefix Dag sealed to a Knot, a fresh suffix epoch continued onto it, folds to the byte-identical supply (1000/300/700, one star vega) as the whole history from empty — checked by a deep states_match (issued·taxed·the whole reserved-star set, not just count). Both boundaries hold: the Knot at genesis (empty prefix) and the full-prefix Knot (empty suffix).
think Refusals with teeth, each proving an invariant crosses the cut: a Knot corrupted after sealing refuses KnotCorrupt; a suffix tax of 800 past a checkpointed supply of 700 refuses Overdraw; a suffix star already sealed (vega) refuses StarTaken. The overdraw/duplicate facts are built raw (not via append_fact, which probe-folds from empty and would itself refuse them) — sharpening the point that they are lawful only against the checkpointed supply.
obs One red caught in-round: fold.append_fact returns a FoldState (probe-folds from empty), not void — so it cannot build the cross-cut suffix logs (their facts are invalid from empty by design). Built those logs by direct field assignment instead, which is the more honest construction and a clearer proof.
obs Two Rooms honesty held: r1 proves correctness (checkpoint-equivalence + invariants cross the cut). The measured bound-win (a history longer than cord_max_blocks that only checkpoint-and-prune can carry) is r3's named loom round; quorum-agreed checkpoints (a node pruning on a checkpoint it did not compute) reach the Comlink-served serve gate and are held for Keaton — no gate crossed this round. Demo keeper seeds only, no key/funds/network/custody.
loom witness=mycelium_cord_knot_witness supply=700 stars=1 issued=1000 taxed=300 invariants_across_cut=3
file active-designing/20260813-050903_mycelium-cord-knot-checkpoint-exploration.md self-approved design read; fixes the Knot shape, name, and four crux-first rounds
file mycelium/cord_knot.rye r1 — seal a committed Cord to a Knot; continue a next epoch onto it; folds identical to the whole history, invariants cross the cut
file tools/mycelium_cord_knot_witness.rish the crux, both boundaries, three refusals; elder Cord + Mycelium fold both green at their doors
file work-in-progress/REMEMBER.md living edge (Knot arc opened, r1 landed) + git nib
recommend keep-going the Knot arc opens; r2 (the knot travels as format cord-knot-v1), r3 (the measured bound-win loom), r4 (read a real knotted fixture true) are each an agent-doable mechanical lap on a spine now known correct
